// spec: FUN-006, VAR-017
//
// A parameter is an assignment context, so a top-level subprogram's declared
// parameter types are enforced exactly as a method's are.
//
// ⚠️ Only the ARITY used to be checked here.  Signature comparison ran only
// when the callee had an owner -- that is, only for a method -- so a top-level
// subprogram fell through to the arity check and its annotation was a contract
// in one place and decoration in the other.  Two dispatch paths behind one
// 'if', where the language has one rule.

function G (N : Integer); begin Exit N; end

WriteLn (G ('a string'));
